ICO">L32B439:40</classification-symbol><classification-symbol scheme="ICO">L32B553:00</classification-symbol> </classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="EN">METHOD OF MANUFACTURING PACKAGING LAMINATE</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb"  status="new" lang="FR">PROCEDE DE FABRICATION DE LAMINE D'EMBALLAGE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-50104280-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>50104280</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5031850-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5031850</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7080989-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7080989</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1177891A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKENOYA TADAKATU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TETRA PAK JAPAN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKENOYA, TADAKATU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIHON TETRA PAK K.K.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKENOYA TADAKATU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKENOYA, TADAKATU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of manufacturing a packaging laminate including aluminum foil; specifically, a method of manufacturing a laminate free from delamination and most suitable for packaging, comprising the steps of coating the innermost film surface of polyolefin with an adhesive resin, pasting aluminum foil using a dry-lamination adhesive, taking up an elongated laminate on a reel for aging, pulling out the resulting laminate from the reel, subjecting the aluminum foil surface to corona discharging, subjecting molten polyolefin to extrusion lamination, and laminating a fibrous carrier layer, whereby the inter-layer adhesion strength of the laminate is improved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de fabrication d'un laminé d'emballage comprenant une feuille d'aluminium. Elle porte notamment sur un procédé de fabrication d'un laminé exempt de délamination et idéal pour l'emballage. Ledit procédé consiste à revêtir d'une résine adhésive la surface du film de polyoléfine la plus à l'intérieur, à coller la feuille d'aluminium au moyen d'un adhésif de contre-collage à sec, un laminé allongé étant enroulé sur une bobine pour subir un vieillissement, à dérouler de la bobine le laminé résultant, à exposer la surface de la feuille d'aluminium à une décharge par effet couronne, à faire subir une extrusion-laminage à la polyoléfine en fusion, et à laminer la couche de support fibreuse, la force d'adhésion entre les couches du laminé étant augmentée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title